Robert Burns Woodward :: Honors and awards :: Honorary degrees :: chunk_0010
Woodward also received over twenty [honorary degrees](/wiki/Honorary_degrees "Honorary degrees"),[[3]](#cite_note-:1-3) including honorary doctorates from the following universities:

* [Wesleyan University](/wiki/Wesleyan_University "Wesleyan University") in 1945;
* [Harvard University](/wiki/Harvard_University "Harvard University") in 1957;
* [University of Cambridge](/wiki/University_of_Cambridge "University of Cambridge") in 1964;
* [Brandeis University](/wiki/Brandeis_University "Brandeis University") in 1965;
* [Technion Israel Institute of Technology](/wiki/Technion_Israel_Institute_of_Technology "Technion Israel Institute of Technology") in [Haifa](/wiki/Haifa "Haifa") in 1966;
* [University of Western Ontario](/wiki/University_of_Western_Ontario "University of Western Ontario") in Canada in 1968;
* [University of Louvain](/wiki/Universit%C3%A9_catholique_de_Louvain "Université catholique de Louvain") in Belgium, 1970.

In 1938, he married Irja Pullman; they had two daughters: Siiri Anna (b. 1939) and Jean Kirsten (b. 1944). In 1946, he married [Eudoxia Muller](/wiki/Eudoxia_Woodward "Eudoxia Woodward"), an artist and technician whom he met at [the Polaroid Corp.](/wiki/Polaroid_Corporation "Polaroid Corporation") This marriage, which lasted until 1972, produced a daughter, and a son: Crystal Elisabeth (b. 1947), and Eric Richard Arthur (b. 1953).[[6]](#cite_note-:0-6)
